*Summary:*

# The documents are mainly focused on the protection of confidential information (including its destruction), and in relation to personal data, they generally indicate that Bolt must comply with the applicable law i.e.:

{quote}_Your company is obliged to ensure that all applicable and effective protection legislation is complied with in your area of operation, including by third parties persons you engage to process personal data for Lidl. In particular, your company undertakes to make its employees aware of the relevant data protection legislation and to undertake in writing to respect the confidentiality of personal data processed for Lidl with which they come into when processing personal data for Lidl._{quote}

# It also includes the following important provision:

{quote} _In the event that your company processes personal data for Lidl on the basis of the instruction,_ *_your company will enter into a personal data processing agreement with Lidl_*_, which will regulate the rights and obligations of your company and Lidl in such personal data processing._{quote}

*Important to note here* - Bolt does not act as a processor processing personal data on the instruction of its customers. This means that we will not need to enter into a separate agreement, and will be able to rely on standard clause 4 of Bolt’s Business T&Cs.

{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}
IF we win the tender and Lidl gets to us with a request to sign a separate data sharing agreement, not agreeing to rely on our clause 4 of BB T&Cs, please escalate to me.
{panel}

Hi [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] below is the draft the response to the German rider, please note that the fragment about the automated decision-making was taken directly from the [German Privacy Passenger Notice|https://bolt.eu/de-de/privacy/privacy-for-riders/?category=rides] 🙂 

Dear Elias,

Thank you for your data subject rights request, which we received on *1 April 2025*.

At Bolt, we take your privacy seriously and are committed to being transparent about our data handling practices, please find the answers to you questions below: 

*Information on the processing of your personal data by Bolt*

For information on how we process your personal data, please check our Privacy Notice available at[ |https://bolt.eu/en-gb/privacy/privacy-for-drivers/?category=rides][https://bolt.eu/de-de/privacy/|https://bolt.eu/de-de/privacy/|smart-link] , which includes further information about:

* The categories of personal data we process;
* The purposes for which we process personal data;
* The recipients or categories of recipients to whom the personal data has been or will be disclosed;
* The criteria we use to determine how long to retain personal data;
* The sources of personal data received from other parties;
* Your rights in relation to your personal data;
* The existence and envisaged consequences of any automated decision-making / profiling of personal data; and
* Details of any transfer of your personal data to third countries or international organisations and the safeguards used for any such transfers.

In addition to the above, please note the following:

* For a list of the Bolt companies and partners with whom we may share your personal data, we refer you to our list of controllers available at [https://bolt.eu/de-de/privacy/privacy-for-riders/?category=rides|https://bolt.eu/de-de/privacy/privacy-for-riders/?category=rides|smart-link] .
* Bolt may share your personal data with the following recipients:
** Drivers;
** Bolt group companies and partners;
** Bolt Business customers and other passengers;
** Insurance companies;
** Law enforcement, data protection, tax, transport and licensing authorities;
** Third-party service providers;
** Data storage providers including *Amazon Web Services EMEA SARL* (38 Avenue John F. Kennedy L-1855 Luxembourg);
* If we transfer your personal data outside of the European Economic Area (EEA), we take appropriate steps to ensure an appropriate level of protection is in place for that personal data in line with applicable legal requirements and rely on the following transfer mechanisms:
** We will rely on decisions from the European Commission where they recognise that certain countries and territories outside of the European Economic Area ensure an adequate level of protection for personal information. 
** We will use standard contractual clauses approved by the European Commission for transfers outside the EEA.
** There also may be certain situations (such as responding to law enforcement requests) where a transfer of personal data will take place on the basis of exemptions provided for under applicable data protection legislation. In these circumstances, we will take steps to minimise and protect the personal data transferred.

*Automated Decision-Making* 

While Bolt may use automated processes for fraud detection, decisions to block a passenger are made after human review by our staff, and no account will be automatically blocked without first completing a verification process.

Bolt retains your personal data only as long as is necessary to provide you with the Bolt services and for the purposes set out in our privacy notice. 

*Average Rating* 

Regarding the creation of a 'profile', we have created a user account for you on our platform based on the information you provided to us when you signed up and information generated through your use of our services (e.g., trip history). This account allows you to access and use our rider services.

Concerning the concept of a 'score' value, we do not assign a general 'score' value to your person. However, we do have an *average rider rating*, which is calculated as an average rating based on your ratings from the previous 365 days. Each rating is from 1 to 5, as provided by the driver at the end of each trip..Your current average rider rating is visible to you within your app. 

*Your rights* 

In addition to your right to access any personal data we hold about you, you have the right to request us to rectify, erase your personal data, restrict the processing of your personal data or to object to such processing. Any such requests that are received will be considered in conjunction with the applicable provisions of relevant data protection laws. 



If you are dissatisfied with this response to your request or in relation to any other matter relating to the processing of your personal data, we hope you will continue to work with us to resolve them. You also have the right to complain directly to your data protection/supervisory authority and, depending on the applicable data protection laws in your country, to seek a judicial remedy.

 

If you have any additional questions, please contact our Customer Support Team by replying to this email.





Yours sincerely,



Bolt

