Dear Elias,

Thank you for your data subject rights request, which we received on 1 April 2025.

For information on how we process relevant personal data, we refer you to our privacy notice available at [https://bolt.eu/de-de/privacy/privacy-for-riders/?category=rides|https://bolt.eu/de-de/privacy/privacy-for-riders/?category=rides], which in particular contains information on:

* The categories of personal data that we process (please also note that you are entitled to request a copy of your personal data processed by Bolt at any time);
* The purposes for which we process personal data;
* The sources of personal data;
* The recipients or categories of recipients to whom the personal data has been or will be disclosed;
* Applicable retention periods for the personal data that we process, including the criteria we use to determine how long to retain personal data; and
* The existence and envisaged consequences of any automated decision-making / profiling.

In addition to the above, please note the following:

* You have created a user account on our platform. This account contains: (i) information you have provided to us ; (ii) information generated through your use of Bolt’s services; and (iii) any applicable information provided by third parties. Your account is currently active, and so you are able to access its contents at any time.
* Bolt may share your personal data with the following recipients or categories of recipients:
** Drivers for the provision of transport services;
** Bolt Group of Companies and partners (for a list of the Bolt companies and partners with whom we may share your personal data, we refer you to our list of controllers available at [https://bolt.eu/de-de/privacy/privacy-controller-list/?category=rides|https://bolt.eu/de-de/privacy/privacy-controller-list/?category=rides]);
** Law enforcement authorities and data protection authorities for administrative or criminal investigation or in relation to legal or data protection claims;
** Payment Providers: *Apple, Inc.,* One Apple Park Way, Cupertino, California _(via the payment service provider - Adyen N.V.);_ *Google Payment Corp*., 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway Mountain View, CA 94043 United States _(via the payment service provider - Adyen N.V.);_ *Adyen N.V.,* Simon Carmiggeltstraat 6, 1011 DJ, Amsterdam; *PayPal Inc.*, San Jose, 2211 N 1st St, United States; *Checkout SAS,* 37-39 rue de Surène, Paris (75008), France;
** Data Storage Providers: *Amazon Web Services EMEA SARL,* 38 Avenue John F. Kennedy L-1855 Luxembourg;
** Support Services Providers: *OpenAI OpCo, LLC,* 3180 18th St., San Francisco, CA 94110, United States for the generation of an automated response for complaint resolution before a human can review; and
** For analytics purposes, we also share user identifiers with the following recipients: *Adyen N.V.* (Amsterdam); *Appsflyer, Inc* (California, United States); *WizRocket, Inc (Clevertap)* (California, United States); *Firebase, Inc* (United States); *Google Ireland Limited* (Ireland); and *Mixpanel, Inc.* (with whom we additionally share: screen views, user events and user properties) (San Francisco, United States).
* {color:#ff5630}Bolt may use automated processes for the purposes of fraud detection and prevention, detecting violations of our platform terms, and applying suspensions and blocks as needed. Such processes either: (a) rely on relevant exceptions under applicable data protection laws and regulations; (b) do not produce legal or similarly significant effects on individuals; or (c) are subject to human review.{color}
* Your Rider Rating (as it appears in your Bolt app) is calculated as an average rating based on your ratings from the previous 365 days. Each rating is from 1 to 5, as provided by the driver at the end of each trip. Further information on Rider Ratings can be found here: [https://bolt.eu/de-de/rider-rating/|https://bolt.eu/de-de/rider-rating/].

*(3) Your rights*

You have the right to request rectification or erasure of personal data or restriction of processing of personal data concerning you or to object to such processing. Any such requests that are received will be considered in conjunction with the applicable provisions of relevant data protection laws. 

If you are dissatisfied with this response to your request or in relation to any other matter relating to the processing of your personal data, we hope you will continue to work with us to resolve them. You have the right to complain directly to the appropriate supervisory authority and seek a judicial remedy. 

If you have any additional questions, please let us know.

Yours sincerely,

*Bolt*

