Hi [~accountid:712020:459f4dab-1b84-4b5a-8aec-5b1cfceef16b] - coming back to you on your questions relating to the banner / newsletter / push notifications

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Can we share details about the promotion via newsletter to all users in Croatia, regardless of whether they are eligible?*
{panel}

If the newsletter is being sent to users *_via direct channels_*, we can only send this to *_Croatian users that have consented to ‘Partner Offers’ in the Bolt app_* ⚠️  

* This is because, where we are sending third-party marketing (as is the case here) to users via +_direct_+ channels, it is caught by direct marketing requirements under applicable law. These requirements include: (i) making sure that the user has consented to receiving such materials; and (ii) providing users with a proper means of opting-out. As such, we should +*not*+ be promoting this via newsletter to any user that has not consented in this way or opted-out (i.e., we cannot send this to all users indiscriminately) where it sent via direct channels. 

If the newsletter is *_not_* being sent to users via direct channels (e.g., it will be passively posted in the background of the Bolt app), this will not be caught by direct marketing requirements - in which case, we could proceed with the proposed approach.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Can we send push notifications about the promotion to all users in Croatia?*
{panel}

We can only send this to *_Croatian users that have consented to ‘Partner Offers’ in the Bolt app_* ⚠️  

* This is for similar reasons as above, as we are using direct channels to send this to users, meaning direct marketing requirements under applicable law are triggered. Admittedly, the *_enforcement and legal risks are lower here_* (as users tend not to complain as much about push notifications, and they have easy means of turning them off), and so it is open to the business to decide whether to proceed with this approach - however, for the reasons set out above, the risk still exists.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Can we place a banner in the app that’s visible to all Croatian users, even if the discount applies only to ZABA cardholders?*
{panel}

Yes - we can. (/) 

Since this is not being sent _directly_ to users (but instead is being passively posted on the app as a form of mass marketing), this will not be caught by direct marketing requirements. As such, we do not need to worry about consent / opt-out obligations here.

